// Layer_Model_Lifecycle — Model Lifecycle Layer
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "Layer_Model_Lifecycle".
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/Layer_Model_Lifecycle.png
// Icons: product logos from docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked 2026-07-11):
//   mlflow, argo, mysql, postgres, minio, prometheus, clickhouse; the rest use
//   generic icons.
//   Metadata and artifact edges follow the data write direction; KFP <> Katib is
//   bidirectional because HPO experiments return trial results to the pipeline.
// Reference: subsec:lapisan-model (Section IV.3, sec:arsitektur-terintegrasi); the
//   first figure for the layer on row 5 of tab:layanan_industri (training part; the
//   model serving part is in Layer_Model_Serving), detailing Figure fig:integrate-service.
//   Included in LaTeX as fig:layer-lifecycle.
// Focus: Feast (training features) > Kubeflow Pipelines (training orchestration, MySQL
//   metadata) + Katib (tuning); MLflow (tracking + model registry, PostgreSQL backend,
//   MinIO artifacts); drift loop verified against the implementation on 2026-07-15:
//   Drift Detector (platform/services/quality/drift, CronJobs drift-check-minute/
//   hourly/daily) reads the feature window from ClickHouse features.data_features,
//   writes PSI + KS to gold.drift_multi_scale; Argo CronWorkflow retrain-on-drift
//   (use-case-crypto/manifests/base/workflows/retrain-on-drift.yaml, schedule
//   "0 */6 * * *") POLLS that table and POSTs to the KFP API, then pushes trigger
//   metrics to Pushgateway. Prometheus is therefore a SINK, not the trigger source,
//   and Evidently is a report UI (evidently ui, fed by platform/services/
//   drift-reporter), not the detector.
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right): left-to-right chain, at most two
//   node rows per group, so the diagram spreads wide and fits the band
//   height=0.42\textheight. Included without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Layer grounding: the group label carries its source category (najafabadi2024analysis),
//   namely ML training plus model registry and ML metadata.
// Implementation check: nodes exist under platform/components/model-lifecycle/
//   (feast, kubeflow-pipelines, kubeflow-katib, kubeflow-notebooks, kubeflow-trainer,
//   mlflow), observability/evidently, observability/kube-prometheus-stack. Argo
//   Workflows/CronWorkflow is the built-in Kubeflow Pipelines execution engine (with no
//   standalone component directory).

direction right

// Feature source (boundary)
Feature Service Layer [icon: package, color: green, label: "Feature Service Layer (Feast, Valkey, Qdrant)"]

// Model Lifecycle Layer
Model Lifecycle Layer [icon: refresh-cw, color: purple, label: "Model Lifecycle Layer (ML training + model registry + ML metadata)"] {
  Kubeflow Notebooks [icon: book-open, label: "Kubeflow Notebooks"]
  Kubeflow Pipelines [icon: workflow, label: "Kubeflow Pipelines (training orchestration)"]
  Katib [icon: sliders, label: "Katib (HPO)"]
  Kubeflow Trainer [icon: cpu, label: "Kubeflow Trainer"]
  MLflow [icon: mlflow, label: "MLflow (tracking + registry)"]
  Argo Workflows [icon: argo, label: "Argo Workflows (CronWorkflow)"]
}

// Metadata and artifact stores (boundary)
MySQL [icon: mysql, color: green, label: "MySQL (KFP + Katib metadata)"]
PostgreSQL [icon: postgres, color: green, label: "PostgreSQL (MLflow backend)"]
MinIO [icon: minio, color: green, label: "MinIO (MLflow artifacts)"]

// Drift measurement, trigger, and consumer (boundary)
ClickHouse [icon: clickhouse, color: green, label: "ClickHouse (feature window + gold.drift_multi_scale)"]
Drift Detector [icon: activity, color: teal, label: "Drift Detector (PSI + KS CronJob)"]
Evidently [icon: monitor, color: teal, label: "Evidently (drift report UI)"]
Prometheus [icon: prometheus, color: teal, label: "Prometheus (via Pushgateway)"]
Model Serving [icon: send, color: red, label: "Model Serving (KServe, separate figure)"]

// Experiment and training flow
Feature Service Layer > Kubeflow Pipelines: training features
Kubeflow Notebooks > Kubeflow Pipelines: experiment to pipeline
Kubeflow Pipelines <> Katib: HPO
Kubeflow Pipelines > Kubeflow Trainer: training job
Kubeflow Pipelines > MLflow: run logging + model registration

// Metadata and artifacts (data write direction)
Kubeflow Pipelines > MySQL: pipeline metadata
Katib > MySQL: tuning metadata
MLflow > PostgreSQL: run metadata
MLflow > MinIO: model artifacts

// Registry to serving
MLflow > Model Serving: model from registry

// Drift-driven automated retraining flow. The Argo CronWorkflow polls
//   ClickHouse on a 6h schedule; nothing pushes to it. Prometheus is a sink
//   (Pushgateway), not the trigger source.
ClickHouse > Drift Detector: feature window
Drift Detector > ClickHouse: PSI + KS scores
ClickHouse > Evidently: drift report source
ClickHouse > Argo Workflows: drift score poll (6h)
Argo Workflows > Kubeflow Pipelines: retraining run
Argo Workflows > Prometheus: trigger metrics
